<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>\mathbf{a} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 1 \\ 2 \\ 2 \end{array}\right)}</m>. Give a vector that is parallel to <m>\mathbf{a}</m> and has magnitude <m>{9}</m>.</p><div><fillin characters="3" name="ans1"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p><m>|\mathbf{a}| = \sqrt{({1})^2 + ({2})^2 + ({2})^2} = {3}</m>. A parallel vector is <m>k\mathbf{a}</m>, with magnitude <m>|k| \times {3}</m>. For magnitude <m>{9}</m>, <m>|k| = {3}</m>, so the vector is <m>{\left(\begin{array}{c} 3 \\ 6 \\ 6 \end{array}\right)}</m> or <m>{\left(\begin{array}{c} -3 \\ -6 \\ -6 \end{array}\right)}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left(\begin{array}{c} 3 \\ 6 \\ 6 \end{array}\right)</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>